# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Group Hamiltonian terms {#2-group-hamiltonian-terms}"
msgstr "2. Regrouper les termes de l'hamiltonien {#2-group-hamiltonian-terms}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the many symmetries that are present in the electronic structure Hamiltonian by grouping related terms that have identical coefficients. This action changes the operator coefficient distribution that the qDRIFT protocol samples from, but it does not affect its convergence guarantees. Crucially, grouping terms that are related by symmetry results in a favorable cancellation of Pauli terms, resulting in an overall shorter circuit depth when time evolving a state under their action.\n"
msgstr "Exploite les nombreuses symétries présentes dans l'hamiltonien de structure électronique en regroupant les termes liés qui ont des coefficients identiques. Cette action modifie la distribution des coefficients de l'opérateur à partir de laquelle le protocole qDRIFT échantillonne, mais n'affecte pas ses garanties de convergence. Surtout, regrouper les termes liés par symétrie entraîne une annulation favorable des termes de Pauli, d'où une profondeur de circuit globalement plus courte lors de l'évolution temporelle d'un état sous leur action.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping` module provides convenience functions for grouping an operator’s terms. This is explained in more detail in [this guide](grouping#grouping-explanation).\n"
msgstr "Le module `qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping` fournit des fonctions pratiques pour regrouper les termes d'un opérateur. Cela est expliqué plus en détail dans [ce guide](grouping#grouping-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Caution\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The implementation of the `group_terms_by_electronic_structure()` assumes the terms of the Hamiltonian to be normal-ordered!\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Attention\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  L'implémentation de `group_terms_by_electronic_structure()` suppose que les termes de l'hamiltonien sont en ordre normal !\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping import group_terms_by_electronic_structure\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.ordering import canonical_order\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> canon = canonical_order(hamil.normal_ordered().simplify(atol=1e-16))\n"
"    >>> exit_code = group_terms_by_electronic_structure(canon, num_modes, two_body_physicist_order=False)\n"
"    >>> assert exit_code is None\n"
"    >>> print(canon.groups)  # the groups attribute now contains some list of group indices\n"
"    [0, ...]\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    QfFermionOperator* normal = qf_ferm_op_normal_ordered(hamil, NULL);\n"
"    QfFermionOperator* simplified = qf_ferm_op_simplify(normal, 1e-16);\n"
"    QfFermionOperator* canon = qf_ferm_op_canonical_order(simplified);\n"
"    QfExitCode exit = qf_ferm_op_group_terms_by_electronic_structure(canon, num_modes, false);\n"
"    assert(exit == QfExitCode_Success);\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    qf_ferm_op_free(normal);\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(simplified);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    qf_ferm_op_free(normal);\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(simplified);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Hint\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Astuce\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The full electronic structure Hamiltonian contains certain terms whose inclusion in a time-evolution circuit has no impact on the perceived bitstrings and, thus, only results in an increased sampling overhead. Therefore, it is recommended that such terms be filtered from the Hamiltonian at this point, before constructing the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate in the next step.\n"
msgstr "  L'hamiltonien de structure électronique complet contient certains termes dont l'inclusion dans un circuit d'évolution temporelle n'a aucun effet sur les chaînes de bits perçues et n'entraîne donc qu'un surcoût d'échantillonnage accru. Il est donc recommandé de filtrer ces termes de l'hamiltonien à ce stade, avant de construire la porte [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") à l'étape suivante.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The terms that fit this description are those that are diagonal in the occupation-number basis, that is, the products of number operators ($a^\\dagger_i a_i$). This includes the constant energy offset, whose time evolution only introduces a global phase into the circuit, the individual number operators whose time evolution amounts to single-qubit Z rotations, as well as higher-order products such as $n_i n_j$. None of them can change a mode’s occupation, so dropping them costs no excitation content. Unlike the per-draw rejection in step 5, this filtering happens once, on the Hamiltonian itself, so the coefficient distribution the protocol samples from is rebuilt consistently from the filtered operator rather than renormalized mid-draw.\n"
msgstr "  Les termes correspondant à cette description sont ceux qui sont diagonaux dans la base des nombres d'occupation, c'est-à-dire les produits d'opérateurs nombre ($a^\\dagger_i a_i$). Cela inclut le décalage d'énergie constant, dont l'évolution temporelle n'introduit qu'une phase globale dans le circuit, les opérateurs nombre individuels dont l'évolution temporelle revient à des rotations Z à un qubit, ainsi que des produits d'ordre supérieur tels que $n_i n_j$. Aucun d'eux ne peut modifier l'occupation d'un mode ; les supprimer ne coûte donc aucun contenu d'excitation. Contrairement au rejet par tirage de l'étape 5, ce filtrage a lieu une seule fois, sur l'hamiltonien lui-même ; la distribution des coefficients dont le protocole échantillonne est donc reconstruite de façon cohérente à partir de l'opérateur filtré, au lieu d'être renormalisée en cours de tirage.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The [`filter_diagonal_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-filter-diagonal-terms#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms\") function removes such terms from an operator in place:\n"
msgstr "  La fonction [`filter_diagonal_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-filter-diagonal-terms#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms\") supprime ces termes d'un opérateur sur place :\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  <Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"<TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"
msgstr ""
"  <Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"<TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"
msgstr "<TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"  </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Filtering here, once, is considerably cheaper than filtering repeatedly. [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") runs once per transpiled circuit, so filtering the Hamiltonian initially, rather than on every call, avoids redoing work for every circuit generated from it.\n"
msgstr "  Filtrer ici, une seule fois, est considérablement moins coûteux que filtrer de manière répétée. [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") s'exécute une fois par circuit transpilé ; filtrer l'hamiltonien au départ, plutôt qu'à chaque appel, évite donc de refaire le travail pour chaque circuit généré à partir de lui.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  For the same reason, it pays to order the Hamiltonian’s terms by group index here. Group indices are a per-term tag that says nothing about where those terms sit, so a group’s terms are in general scattered throughout the operator: the grouping applied above assigns indices in order of first encounter, which leaves a group’s second term far from its first.\n"
msgstr "  Pour la même raison, il est avantageux d'ordonner ici les termes de l'hamiltonien par indice de groupe. Les indices de groupe sont une étiquette par terme qui ne dit rien de la position de ces termes ; les termes d'un groupe sont donc en général dispersés dans l'opérateur : le regroupement appliqué plus haut attribue les indices dans l'ordre de première rencontre, ce qui laisse le deuxième terme d'un groupe loin du premier.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") samples whole groups and looks each drawn group up with [`split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups\"). Finding a group among scattered terms means scanning all of them, so that lookup costs the same whether one group is drawn or forty. [`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_order\") gathers each group into one contiguous run, after which a lookup is a binary search over the group boundaries and costs what the *drawn* groups cost rather than what the *held* terms cost. The lookup itself becomes dramatically cheaper; how much of a given transpilation that saves depends on what else the pipeline does, since mapping and synthesis dominate once the scan is gone:\n"
msgstr "  [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") échantillonne des groupes entiers et recherche chaque groupe tiré avec [`split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.split_out_groups\"). Trouver un groupe parmi des termes dispersés oblige à les parcourir tous, de sorte que cette recherche coûte autant qu'on tire un groupe ou quarante. [`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_order\") rassemble chaque groupe en une séquence contiguë, après quoi une recherche est une recherche binaire sur les frontières des groupes et coûte ce que coûtent les groupes *tirés* plutôt que les termes *détenus*. La recherche elle-même devient considérablement moins chère ; la part que cela représente dans une transpilation donnée dépend de ce que fait d'autre le pipeline, car le mapping et la synthèse dominent une fois le parcours supprimé :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This reorders the terms without changing the operator’s value, and needs to happen only once no matter how many circuit randomizations are drawn from it.\n"
msgstr "  Cela réordonne les termes sans changer la valeur de l'opérateur, et n'a besoin d'avoir lieu qu'une seule fois, quel que soit le nombre de randomisations de circuit tirées à partir de lui.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"prepare-the-time-evolution-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Prepare the time evolution circuit {#3-prepare-the-time-evolution-circuit}"
msgstr "3. Préparer le circuit d'évolution temporelle {#3-prepare-the-time-evolution-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the Hamiltonian’s time evolution circuit and the base circuit from which to draw samples. The [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") contains all the required components to do so, in compliance with Qiskit conventions.\n"
msgstr "Prépare le circuit d'évolution temporelle de l'hamiltonien et le circuit de base à partir duquel tirer les échantillons. Le module [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") contient tous les composants nécessaires pour cela, conformément aux conventions de Qiskit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The qDRIFT protocol is the synthesis method [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\"), and the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate carries it as its [`synthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-gate#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate.synthesis \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate.synthesis\"). The method introduces the few parameters you can use to customize the circuits to generate:\n"
msgstr "Le protocole qDRIFT est la méthode de synthèse [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\"), et la porte [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") la porte comme sa [`synthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-gate#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate.synthesis \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicGate.synthesis\"). La méthode introduit les quelques paramètres que tu peux utiliser pour personnaliser les circuits à générer :\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The length of each circuit in terms of excitation groups: `num_groups`\n"
msgstr "La longueur de chaque circuit en nombre de groupes d'excitations : `num_groups`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optionally, a seed for the random number generator: `rng`\n"
msgstr "Facultativement, une graine pour le générateur de nombres aléatoires : `rng`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optionally, precomputed sampling weights, if the transpilation itself becomes a bottleneck: `weights` (see [(Optional) Precompute the sampling weights](#sqdrift-sampling-weights) below)\n"
msgstr "Facultativement, des poids d'échantillonnage précalculés, si la transpilation elle-même devient un goulot d'étranglement : `weights` (voir [(Facultatif) Précalculer les poids d'échantillonnage](#sqdrift-sampling-weights) ci-dessous)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the method is held by the gate, whatever describes the gate’s operator, such as those weights, sits right next to that operator.\n"
msgstr "Comme la méthode est portée par la porte, tout ce qui décrit l'opérateur de la porte, comme ces poids, se trouve juste à côté de cet opérateur.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit import FermionicCircuit\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit.library import Evolution\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis import FermionicQDrift\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> time = 1.0  # you can choose a desired scaling factor here\n"
"    >>> num_groups = 10\n"
"    >>> qdrift = FermionicQDrift(num_groups, rng=19)\n"
"    >>> evo_gate = Evolution(num_modes, canon, time, synthesis=qdrift)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> circ = FermionicCircuit(num_modes)\n"
"    >>> circ.append(evo_gate, circ.modes)\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // WARNING: Qiskit's C API does not yet allow us to implement circuits\n"
"    // with custom gate definitions.\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  This example neither initializes the fermionic modes with particles, nor measures their final state.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Cet exemple n'initialise pas les modes fermioniques avec des particules et ne mesure pas non plus leur état final.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpile-the-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Transpile the circuit {#4-transpile-the-circuit}"
msgstr "4. Transpiler le circuit {#4-transpile-the-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`qiskit_fermions.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler#module-qiskit_fermions.transpiler \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler\") module integrates directly with Qiskit’s transpilation pipeline, allowing the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") constructed above to be directly transpiled to a [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit).\n"
msgstr "Le module [`qiskit_fermions.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler#module-qiskit_fermions.transpiler \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler\") s'intègre directement au pipeline de transpilation de Qiskit, ce qui permet de transpiler directement en [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) le [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") construit plus haut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") fermion-to-qubit mapping to convert the Hamiltonian expressed in terms of fermions to be expressed in Pauli strings instead. This can be done directly as part of the transpilation process by using the [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\") transpilation pass. Use [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") to build `FermionicStagedPassManager`, which ensures that the Jordan-Wigner encoding is used consistently for all circuit instructions.\n"
msgstr "Utilise le mapping fermion-vers-qubit [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") pour convertir l'hamiltonien exprimé en fermions en chaînes de Pauli. Cela peut se faire directement dans le processus de transpilation grâce à la passe de transpilation [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\"). Utilise [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") pour construire `FermionicStagedPassManager`, qui garantit que l'encodage de Jordan-Wigner est utilisé de façon cohérente pour toutes les instructions du circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Crucially, add Qiskit’s [`Decompose`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Decompose) pass to the `optimization` stage of the transpilation pipeline. It breaks the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate down with the synthesis method the gate carries, which is the qDRIFT method prepared above. This ensures that the circuit does not use the time evolution of the entire Hamiltonian, whose depth would exceed the capabilities of currently available quantum computing hardware.\n"
msgstr "Surtout, ajoute la passe [`Decompose`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Decompose) de Qiskit à l'étape `optimization` du pipeline de transpilation. Elle décompose la porte [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") avec la méthode de synthèse que porte la porte, c'est-à-dire la méthode qDRIFT préparée plus haut. Cela garantit que le circuit n'utilise pas l'évolution temporelle de l'hamiltonien entier, dont la profondeur dépasserait les capacités du matériel de calcul quantique actuellement disponible.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead, it subsamples a fixed number of `groups` of Hamiltonian terms for each circuit, every time the circuit is transpiled. Through this, you can generate multiple circuit randomizations as required by the [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) algorithm by repeatedly running the transpilation pipeline. The number of circuits to generate is `num_sqdrift_randomizations`.\n"
msgstr "À la place, elle sous-échantillonne un nombre fixe de `groups` de termes de l'hamiltonien pour chaque circuit, à chaque transpilation du circuit. Ainsi, tu peux générer plusieurs randomisations de circuit, comme l'exige l'algorithme [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578), en exécutant à plusieurs reprises le pipeline de transpilation. Le nombre de circuits à générer est `num_sqdrift_randomizations`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit.transpiler.passes import Decompose\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.transpiler import FermionicPassManager\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets import generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> pm = generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()\n"
"    >>> pm.optimization = FermionicPassManager([Decompose([\"Evolution\"])])\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> num_sqdrift_randomizations = 10\n"
"    >>> sqdrift_circuits = [\n"
"    ...     pm.run(circ) for _ in range(num_sqdrift_randomizations)\n"
"    ... ]\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // WARNING: Qiskit's C API does not yet allow us to implement circuits\n"
"    // with custom gate definitions, which we therefore also cannot transpile\n"
"    // via this API.\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The preceding examples fix the `rng` seed of the [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") synthesis method, so that the sequence of randomizations can be reproduced.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Les exemples précédents fixent la graine `rng` de la méthode de synthèse [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\"), afin que la séquence de randomisations puisse être reproduite.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The same pipeline accepts the qDRIFT method in two other places. The [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") pass takes one method for *every* [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate by name, `F2FSynthesis({\"Evolution\": FermionicQDrift(num_groups)})`, which is all that is needed when no gate holds anything specific to its operator. The next step uses the third one, the [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\") pass.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Astuce\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Le même pipeline accepte la méthode qDRIFT à deux autres endroits. La passe [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") prend une méthode pour *chaque* porte [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") par son nom, `F2FSynthesis({\"Evolution\": FermionicQDrift(num_groups)})`, ce qui suffit quand aucune porte ne détient rien de spécifique à son opérateur. L'étape suivante utilise le troisième endroit, la passe [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"filter-drawn-excitations-by-occupation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Filter drawn excitations by occupation {#5-filter-drawn-excitations-by-occupation}"
msgstr "5. Filtrer les excitations tirées selon l'occupation {#5-filter-drawn-excitations-by-occupation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beyond the diagonal terms filtered out in the previous step, a drawn excitation can act entirely within a set of modes whose occupation is already fixed (all occupied or all unoccupied), where it cannot move a particle from one side to the other. Such an excitation tells you nothing about the sampled bitstrings, so a slot spent on it is a slot wasted. The [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\") pass, which wraps the same [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") method, rejects such excitations as they are drawn and draws a replacement, so that each of the `num_groups` slots of the resulting circuit carries an excitation that couples the two sides.\n"
msgstr "Outre les termes diagonaux filtrés à l'étape précédente, une excitation tirée peut agir entièrement au sein d'un ensemble de modes dont l'occupation est déjà fixée (tous occupés ou tous inoccupés), où elle ne peut pas déplacer une particule d'un côté à l'autre. Une telle excitation ne t'apprend rien sur les chaînes de bits échantillonnées ; un emplacement dépensé pour elle est donc un emplacement gaspillé. La passe [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\"), qui enveloppe la même méthode [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\"), rejette ces excitations au moment du tirage et en tire une de remplacement, de sorte que chacun des `num_groups` emplacements du circuit obtenu porte une excitation qui couple les deux côtés.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  This filtering is not free, and it is a separate pass for that reason. What it conserves is the budget of `num_groups` sampled slots, not the circuit depth: since that budget is fixed, a rejected excitation is replaced rather than dropped, and a cheap one gives way to a coupling excitation that costs more to synthesize. Expect a filtered circuit to be deeper than an unfiltered one drawn from the same seed.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Avertissement\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Ce filtrage n'est pas gratuit, et c'est pourquoi il s'agit d'une passe distincte. Ce qu'il conserve, c'est le budget de `num_groups` emplacements échantillonnés, pas la profondeur du circuit : ce budget étant fixe, une excitation rejetée est remplacée et non supprimée, et une excitation peu coûteuse cède la place à une excitation de couplage qui coûte plus cher à synthétiser. Attends-toi à ce qu'un circuit filtré soit plus profond qu'un circuit non filtré tiré à partir de la même graine.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Renormalizing the draw over the accepted excitations changes the distribution the qDRIFT protocol samples from, and unlike the grouping in step 2 it also breaks the protocol’s convergence guarantee: the sampled product no longer averages to the evolution under the Hamiltonian you passed in. Every retained excitation ends up weighted by the reciprocal of the acceptance probability, the rejected ones contribute nothing, and neither the total coefficient magnitude nor the per-gate evolution time is adjusted to compensate.\n"
msgstr "  Renormaliser le tirage sur les excitations acceptées modifie la distribution dont le protocole qDRIFT échantillonne et, contrairement au regroupement de l'étape 2, brise aussi la garantie de convergence du protocole : le produit échantillonné ne moyenne plus à l'évolution sous l'hamiltonien que tu as fourni. Chaque excitation retenue finit pondérée par l'inverse de la probabilité d'acceptation, les excitations rejetées ne contribuent à rien, et ni la magnitude totale des coefficients ni le temps d'évolution par porte ne sont ajustés pour compenser.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The acceptance rule is also an over-approximation. It compares mode supports only, so it carries no amplitude information, and the tracked sets only ever grow: an excitation confined to the occupied set is genuinely inert on a product state, but the same reasoning gets weaker for later draws, once earlier accepted excitations have left the state entangled and marked most modes “uncertain”.\n"
msgstr "  La règle d'acceptation est aussi une sur-approximation. Elle ne compare que les supports de modes, elle ne porte donc aucune information d'amplitude, et les ensembles suivis ne font que croître : une excitation confinée à l'ensemble occupé est véritablement inerte sur un état produit, mais le même raisonnement s'affaiblit pour les tirages suivants, une fois que les excitations acceptées précédemment ont intriqué l'état et marqué la plupart des modes comme « incertains ».\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Use the filtering for the bitstring-sampling workflow this guide describes, where the circuits feed SQD post-processing and only the sampled bitstrings matter. Do not use it if you intend to estimate an expectation value from these circuits, or to rely on the qDRIFT error bound in any other way: those results carry a bias that the pass does not correct for.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Utilise le filtrage pour le workflow d'échantillonnage de chaînes de bits que décrit ce guide, où les circuits alimentent le post-traitement SQD et où seules les chaînes de bits échantillonnées comptent. Ne l'utilise pas si tu comptes estimer une valeur moyenne à partir de ces circuits, ou t'appuyer d'une autre façon sur la borne d'erreur de qDRIFT : ces résultats portent un biais que la passe ne corrige pas.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This filtering needs to know which modes start out occupied. It therefore requires an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate preceding the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gates in the circuit; [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") is a convenient way to construct one. Add one here for the N2 Hartree-Fock reference (seven alpha and seven beta electrons in 14 spatial orbitals) and compare the sampled excitations with and without the filtering:\n"
msgstr "Ce filtrage doit savoir quels modes sont initialement occupés. Il exige donc une porte [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") précédant les portes [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") dans le circuit ; [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") est un moyen pratique d'en construire une. Ajoutes-en une ici pour la référence de Hartree-Fock de N2 (sept électrons alpha et sept électrons bêta dans 14 orbitales spatiales) et compare les excitations échantillonnées avec et sans filtrage :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.circuit.library import InitializeModes\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes import F2FSynthesis, QDriftTrotterization\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> init = InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock(fcidump.norb, (7, 7))\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> hf_circ = FermionicCircuit(num_modes)\n"
"    >>> hf_circ.append(init, hf_circ.modes)\n"
"    >>> hf_circ.append(Evolution(num_modes, canon, time), hf_circ.modes)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> num_groups = 5\n"
"    >>> qdrift_unfiltered = F2FSynthesis(\n"
"    ...     {\"Evolution\": FermionicQDrift(num_groups, rng=3480)}\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>> qdrift_trivial = QDriftTrotterization(\n"
"    ...     FermionicQDrift(num_groups, rng=3480)\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> for instruction in FermionicPassManager(qdrift_unfiltered).run(hf_circ)._inner.data:\n"
"    ...     if instruction.operation.name == \"Evolution\":\n"
"    ...         print(sorted(instruction.operation.operator.get_support()))\n"
"    [2, 4]\n"
"    [41, 45, 52]\n"
"    [15, 45, 55]\n"
"    [41, 52, 53]\n"
"    [10, 16, 37, 38]\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> for instruction in FermionicPassManager(qdrift_trivial).run(hf_circ)._inner.data:\n"
"    ...     if instruction.operation.name == \"Evolution\":\n"
"    ...         print(sorted(instruction.operation.operator.get_support()))\n"
"    [0, 1, 6, 7]\n"
"    [0, 1, 28, 29]\n"
"    [4, 13, 55]\n"
"    [13, 20, 40, 41]\n"
"    [0, 1, 28, 29]\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "None of the excitations drawn without filtering touch the occupied set (`0-6` and `28-34`) at all, so none of them can move a particle between an occupied and an unoccupied mode. With the filtering, all five are rejected and replaced by excitations that do couple an occupied mode with an unoccupied one. For example, the first accepted excitation `[0, 1, 6, 7]` moves a particle between occupied modes `0`, `1`, and `6` and unoccupied mode `7`.\n"
msgstr "Aucune des excitations tirées sans filtrage ne touche l'ensemble occupé (`0-6` et `28-34`), si bien qu'aucune ne peut déplacer une particule entre un mode occupé et un mode inoccupé. Avec le filtrage, les cinq sont rejetées et remplacées par des excitations qui couplent bien un mode occupé à un mode inoccupé. Par exemple, la première excitation acceptée `[0, 1, 6, 7]` déplace une particule entre les modes occupés `0`, `1` et `6` et le mode inoccupé `7`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once an excitation is accepted, every mode in its support becomes “uncertain” and, thus, eligible to play either role for later samples, so the occupied and unoccupied mode sets keep growing as more excitations get accepted. This is what makes the second excitation, `[0, 1, 28, 29]`, acceptable. All four of its modes are among the *originally* occupied ones, so it does not couple to any originally unoccupied mode. It is only accepted because modes `0` and `1` became uncertain (and thus eligible as the “unoccupied” side of the coupling) once the first excitation touched them.\n"
msgstr "Dès qu'une excitation est acceptée, chaque mode de son support devient « incertain » et peut donc jouer l'un ou l'autre rôle pour les échantillons suivants ; les ensembles de modes occupés et inoccupés continuent ainsi de croître à mesure que d'autres excitations sont acceptées. C'est ce qui rend acceptable la deuxième excitation, `[0, 1, 28, 29]`. Ses quatre modes figurent parmi ceux qui étaient *à l'origine* occupés, elle ne se couple donc à aucun mode initialement inoccupé. Elle n'est acceptée que parce que les modes `0` et `1` sont devenus incertains (et donc éligibles comme côté « inoccupé » du couplage) une fois touchés par la première excitation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This growth is what makes the rule an over-approximation rather than a test: as more modes turn uncertain, fewer draws are rejected, and the filtering does the most to the sampling distribution on the earliest draws.\n"
msgstr "Cette croissance fait de la règle une sur-approximation plutôt qu'un test : à mesure que davantage de modes deviennent incertains, moins de tirages sont rejetés, et c'est sur les premiers tirages que le filtrage agit le plus sur la distribution d'échantillonnage.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To judge how far the filtering moved the distribution, read the rejection counts the pass records in the circuit metadata. One entry is stored per filtered [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate, and the accepted-to-total ratio estimates the acceptance probability, which is the factor by which the retained excitations were over-weighted:\n"
msgstr "Pour juger de combien le filtrage a déplacé la distribution, lis les comptes de rejets que la passe enregistre dans les métadonnées du circuit. Une entrée est stockée par porte [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") filtrée, et le rapport acceptées sur total estime la probabilité d'acceptation, qui est le facteur par lequel les excitations retenues ont été surpondérées :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> # a freshly seeded pass, so the counts do not depend on earlier draws\n"
"    >>> qdrift_counted = QDriftTrotterization(\n"
"    ...     FermionicQDrift(num_groups, rng=3480)\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>> filtered = FermionicPassManager(qdrift_counted).run(hf_circ)\n"
"    >>> discarded = filtered.metadata.get(\"filter_trivial.discarded\")\n"
"    >>> emitted = filtered.metadata.get(\"filter_trivial.emitted\")\n"
"    >>> print(f\"{emitted[0]} kept, {discarded[0]} discarded\")\n"
"    5 kept, 7 discarded\n"
"    >>> print(f\"acceptance probability: {emitted[0] / (emitted[0] + discarded[0]):.2f}\")\n"
"    acceptance probability: 0.42\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Filtering needs occupation information to filter against. A [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate seeds it just as [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") does, and any [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") marks every mode it acts on as “uncertain”. Without any of them, or when the seeded modes all land on one side (every mode occupied, or every mode unoccupied), the pass emits a [`UserWarning`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#UserWarning) and leaves the sampling unfiltered for that [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate. On a Hamiltonian whose remaining terms can no longer couple the two tracked sets, the pass instead raises [`RuntimeError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#RuntimeError) after [`QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES\") consecutive rejections.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Le filtrage a besoin d'informations d'occupation sur lesquelles filtrer. Une porte [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") les fournit tout comme [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\"), et toute [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") marque comme « incertain » chaque mode sur lequel elle agit. En l'absence de toutes ces portes, ou lorsque les modes initialisés tombent tous du même côté (tous occupés, ou tous inoccupés), la passe émet un [`UserWarning`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#UserWarning) et laisse l'échantillonnage non filtré pour cette porte [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\"). Sur un hamiltonien dont les termes restants ne peuvent plus coupler les deux ensembles suivis, la passe lève à la place une [`RuntimeError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#RuntimeError) après [`QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization.MAX_SAMPLE_RETRIES\") rejets consécutifs.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sqdrift-sampling-weights\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Optional) Precompute the sampling weights {#optional-precompute-the-sampling-weights}"
msgstr "(Facultatif) Précalculer les poids d'échantillonnage {#optional-precompute-the-sampling-weights}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reach for this only if the transpilation itself is a bottleneck. It changes nothing about the circuits you get.\n"
msgstr "N'y recours que si la transpilation elle-même est un goulot d'étranglement. Cela ne change rien aux circuits que tu obtiens.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") draws each group with a probability proportional to the magnitude of its coefficient, and derives those magnitudes from the Hamiltonian on every call: one value per Hamiltonian *term*, reduced down to one per group. Because the method is stateless it repeats that reduction for every randomization, even though the result is identical every time. The `weights` argument lets you compute it once with [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") and hand the result over, moving the cost out of the loop while leaving the method free of any cached, Hamiltonian-dependent state.\n"
msgstr "[`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") tire chaque groupe avec une probabilité proportionnelle à la magnitude de son coefficient, et déduit ces magnitudes de l'hamiltonien à chaque appel : une valeur par *terme* de l'hamiltonien, réduite à une par groupe. Comme la méthode est sans état, elle répète cette réduction pour chaque randomisation, bien que le résultat soit identique à chaque fois. L'argument `weights` te permet de la calculer une seule fois avec [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") et de transmettre le résultat, ce qui sort le coût de la boucle tout en laissant la méthode exempte de tout état mis en cache dépendant de l'hamiltonien.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the counterpart of the term ordering in step 2. That one hoists the group *lookup* out of the loop, this one the weight *reduction*, and each is only as noticeable as the other is absent, so it is worth applying both together. Since `canon` was already reordered above, the two compose directly.\n"
msgstr "C'est la contrepartie de l'ordonnancement des termes de l'étape 2. Celui-ci sort de la boucle la *recherche* de groupe, celui-ci la *réduction* des poids, et chacun n'est sensible que dans la mesure où l'autre est absent ; il vaut donc la peine de les appliquer ensemble. Puisque `canon` a déjà été réordonné plus haut, les deux se composent directement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The weights describe the groups of one particular operator, so they belong with the [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate of that operator: build the method for that gate and hand it over as the gate’s `synthesis`, exactly as in step 3.\n"
msgstr "Les poids décrivent les groupes d'un opérateur particulier ; ils appartiennent donc à la porte [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") de cet opérateur : construis la méthode pour cette porte et transmets-la comme `synthesis` de la porte, exactement comme à l'étape 3.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.grouping import group_coeff_means\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> weights = group_coeff_means(canon)  # `canon` is group-ordered, from step 2\n"
"    >>> qdrift_weighted = FermionicQDrift(10, rng=19, weights=weights)\n"
"    >>> weighted_gate = Evolution(num_modes, canon, time, synthesis=qdrift_weighted)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> weighted_circ = FermionicCircuit(num_modes)\n"
"    >>> weighted_circ.append(weighted_gate, weighted_circ.modes)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> weighted_circuits = [\n"
"    ...     pm.run(weighted_circ) for _ in range(num_sqdrift_randomizations)\n"
"    ... ]\n"
"    >>> len(weighted_circuits)\n"
"    10\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since those are exactly the weights the pass would have computed, the circuits are the same as before; only the repeated reduction is gone.\n"
msgstr "Comme ce sont exactement les poids que la passe aurait calculés, les circuits sont les mêmes qu'avant ; seule la réduction répétée a disparu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One entry is expected per *group*, not per term, whenever the operator carries groups, since a grouped operator is sampled group-wise. Entries must be non-negative: a weight is a *magnitude*, because the qDRIFT protocol decomposes $H = \\sum_j h_j H_j$ with positive $h_j$, and a coefficient’s sign belongs to $H_j$, where the pass reads it off the operator directly.\n"
msgstr "Une entrée est attendue par *groupe*, et non par terme, chaque fois que l'opérateur porte des groupes, puisqu'un opérateur groupé est échantillonné groupe par groupe. Les entrées doivent être non négatives : un poids est une *magnitude*, car le protocole qDRIFT décompose $H = \\sum_j h_j H_j$ avec des $h_j$ positifs, et le signe d'un coefficient appartient à $H_j$, où la passe le lit directement sur l'opérateur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Caution\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The weights are absolute magnitudes, not relative preferences. Their sum also fixes the evolution time, so multiplying every entry by $\\gamma$ samples identically but evolves for $\\gamma t$ instead of $t$. Passing anything other than the Hamiltonian’s own coefficient magnitudes therefore changes which evolution the ensemble approximates, which is why this is a performance tool rather than a way to tune the sampling.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Attention\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Les poids sont des magnitudes absolues, pas des préférences relatives. Leur somme fixe aussi le temps d'évolution, de sorte que multiplier chaque entrée par $\\gamma$ échantillonne de façon identique mais évolue pendant $\\gamma t$ au lieu de $t$. Passer autre chose que les magnitudes de coefficients propres à l'hamiltonien change donc l'évolution que l'ensemble approxime, c'est pourquoi il s'agit d'un outil de performance et non d'un moyen de régler l'échantillonnage.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the weights belong to the gate whose operator they describe, a circuit may hold several [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gates, each with the weights of its own operator. The [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\") pass of step 5 honors them in the same way: it draws a gate with the [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") that the gate carries, and falls back to the one it was constructed with for the gates that carry none. Another kind of synthesis method on a gate is not a statement about qDRIFT, so the pass ignores it. Giving the method to a pass by gate name instead, as in `F2FSynthesis({\"Evolution\": ...})`, applies one method to every [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate, so weights passed there are only meaningful for a circuit with a single one. The length of the weights is checked against each gate they are applied to.\n"
msgstr "Comme les poids appartiennent à la porte dont ils décrivent l'opérateur, un circuit peut contenir plusieurs portes [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\"), chacune avec les poids de son propre opérateur. La passe [`QDriftTrotterization`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-q-drift-trotterization#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.QDriftTrotterization\") de l'étape 5 les respecte de la même façon : elle tire pour une porte avec le [`FermionicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-q-drift#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicQDrift\") que porte cette porte, et se rabat sur celui avec lequel elle a été construite pour les portes qui n'en portent aucun. Un autre type de méthode de synthèse sur une porte n'est pas une déclaration sur qDRIFT, la passe l'ignore donc. Donner la méthode à une passe par nom de porte à la place, comme dans `F2FSynthesis({\"Evolution\": ...})`, applique une seule méthode à chaque porte [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\"), de sorte que des poids passés ainsi n'ont de sens que pour un circuit n'en comportant qu'une. La longueur des poids est vérifiée par rapport à chaque porte à laquelle ils sont appliqués.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Optional) Optimize the fermionic mode indexing {#optional-optimize-the-fermionic-mode-indexing}"
msgstr "(Facultatif) Optimiser l'indexation des modes fermioniques {#optional-optimize-the-fermionic-mode-indexing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can add an additional optimization step to the transpilation pipeline that minimizes the distance of the fermionic excitation spans by relabeling the fermionic mode indices. This optimization was introduced in the [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) paper and is implemented by [`build_excitation_span_minimization_model()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-optimization-build-excitation-span-minimization-model#qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model\"). It can be easily inserted into the transpiler pipeline by using the [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") pass:\n"
msgstr "Tu peux ajouter au pipeline de transpilation une étape d'optimisation supplémentaire qui minimise la distance des étendues d'excitation fermioniques en réétiquetant les indices des modes fermioniques. Cette optimisation a été introduite dans l'article [SqDRIFT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.02578) et est implémentée par [`build_excitation_span_minimization_model()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-optimization-build-excitation-span-minimization-model#qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model\"). Elle peut être facilement insérée dans le pipeline du transpileur grâce à la passe [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from pyomo.environ import SolverFactory\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes import RelabelModes\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> solver = SolverFactory(\"appsi_highs\")\n"
"    >>> solver.options[\"time_limit\"] = 10\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> qdrift = F2FSynthesis({\"Evolution\": FermionicQDrift(5, rng=19)})\n"
"    >>> relabel = RelabelModes(solver=solver)\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> pm.optimization = FermionicPassManager([qdrift, relabel])\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> relabeled_circ = pm.run(circ)\n"
"    >>> # if the automatic mode relabeling was successful, the circuit's\n"
"    >>> # metadata will contain the mode `permutation` information\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // WARNING: This feature is not available via the C API.\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Using the automatic optimization inside [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") (which leverages [`build_excitation_span_minimization_model()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-optimization-build-excitation-span-minimization-model#qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model\")) requires the optional dependency managed by [`HAS_PYOMO`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_PYOMO \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_PYOMO\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  L'utilisation de l'optimisation automatique dans [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") (qui s'appuie sur [`build_excitation_span_minimization_model()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-optimization-build-excitation-span-minimization-model#qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.optimization.build_excitation_span_minimization_model\")) nécessite la dépendance facultative gérée par [`HAS_PYOMO`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_PYOMO \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_PYOMO\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The relabeling changes which mode a given qubit carries, so the subspace diagonalization only gets the right bitstrings if that is accounted for. Where the accounting happens depends on where you measure.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Le réétiquetage change le mode que porte un qubit donné ; la diagonalisation de sous-espace n'obtient donc les bonnes chaînes de bits que si cela est pris en compte. L'endroit où cette prise en compte a lieu dépend de l'endroit où tu mesures.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Add the measurements to the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") with [`FermionicCircuit.measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") before transpiling, and there is nothing to do: each measurement names the mode it reads, so the relabeling carries it along and the sampled bitstrings are indexed by the original mode.\n"
msgstr "  Ajoute les mesures au [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") avec [`FermionicCircuit.measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") avant la transpilation, et il n'y a rien à faire : chaque mesure nomme le mode qu'elle lit, le réétiquetage la porte donc avec lui et les chaînes de bits échantillonnées sont indexées par le mode d'origine.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Measure the transpiled [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) instead, and the bitstrings must be post-processed using the `permutation` recorded in the circuit’s metadata. See the [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") documentation for the recipe.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Si tu mesures plutôt le [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) transpilé, les chaînes de bits doivent être post-traitées à l'aide de la `permutation` enregistrée dans les métadonnées du circuit. Consulte la documentation de [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") pour la marche à suivre.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Prochaines étapes {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that you have successfully generated an ensemble of circuits, you can sample bitstrings from them. To do so, the circuits must be executed on hardware. Refer to the [Qiskit documentation](/guides/intro-to-patterns) for detailed instructions.\n"
msgstr "Maintenant que tu as généré avec succès un ensemble de circuits, tu peux en échantillonner des chaînes de bits. Pour cela, les circuits doivent être exécutés sur du matériel. Consulte la [documentation Qiskit](/guides/intro-to-patterns) pour des instructions détaillées.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once the bitstring samples have been obtained, these can be used in combination with the Hamiltonian coefficients to perform SQD post-processing, as explained in the [SQD addon tutorials](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/overview).\n"
msgstr "Une fois les échantillons de chaînes de bits obtenus, ils peuvent être utilisés avec les coefficients de l'hamiltonien pour effectuer le post-traitement SQD, comme expliqué dans les [tutoriels de l'addon SQD](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/overview).\n"
